Both known shapes are already patched in s02:
- opticon.c: `size_t data_len = urb->actual_length - 2;` occurs BEFORE the `if (urb->actual_length <= 2)` check. Wait — look carefully: 

```c
	const unsigned char *data = hdr + 2;
	size_t data_len = urb->actual_length - 2;

	if (urb->actual_length <= 2) {
		...
		return;
	}
```

The subtraction `urb->actual_length - 2` is computed into size_t data_len before the check. If actual_length is 0 or 1, data_len underflows to huge size_t value. BUT the check returns before data_len is used. So the underflowed value is computed but never used — the check catches it before use. So this is the upstream fixed version? Let me check upstream. Upstream opticon.c after fix:

